WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.480
Welcome to Grade 8 English, Unit 2:
Design, Packaging, and Sustainability.

2
00:00:05.780 --> 00:00:09.180
Welcome to Unit 2 of your Year 8 English course.

3
00:00:09.500 --> 00:00:14.160
In this unit, you will explore the
fascinating world of design, packaging,

4
00:00:14.160 --> 00:00:19.820
and sustainability through the lens of a
powerful story called "Signal in the Static."

5
00:00:20.640 --> 00:00:25.550
This story follows two courageous
Somali students, Samira and Ibrahim,

6
00:00:25.550 --> 00:00:32.900
who run a youth radio station in Hargeisa and use their
platform to investigate a secret land deal that threatens

7
00:00:32.900 --> 00:00:33.980
community gardens.

8
00:00:34.640 --> 00:00:39.640
Their journey will show you how
design thinking, clear communication,

9
00:00:39.640 --> 00:00:44.860
and a commitment to truth can make
a real difference in your community.

10
00:00:45.560 --> 00:00:51.440
In this short lecture, preview the key
ideas and prepare for the independent lesson.

11
00:00:52.100 --> 00:01:00.100
By the end of this unit, you will be able to read and
analyse a narrative text, identifying themes of truth, bias,

12
00:01:00.460 --> 00:01:02.840
manipulation, and civic responsibility.

13
00:01:03.700 --> 00:01:10.390
you will also use partitive expressions correctly
and confidently in both speaking and writing (e.g.,

14
00:01:11.000 --> 00:01:14.880
a piece of evidence, a surge of
indignation, a multitude of voices).

15
00:01:14.880 --> 00:01:23.500
you will also form and use zero and first conditionals
to express general truths and real future possibilities.

16
00:01:24.400 --> 00:01:26.560
Keep these goals in mind as you work.

17
00:01:27.260 --> 00:01:35.020
Your vocabulary work begins with these words:
exult, loathe, usurp, feign, intervene, obstruct.

18
00:01:35.740 --> 00:01:41.040
Listen to each pronunciation in the
vocabulary lab, study its meaning in context,

19
00:01:41.400 --> 00:01:44.860
and use the word accurately in
your own discussion and writing.

20
00:01:45.740 --> 00:01:53.040
The reading sequence includes Design, Packaging, and
Sustainability: source text 1 and Design, Packaging,

21
00:01:53.040 --> 00:01:56.460
and Sustainability: source text 2.

22
00:01:56.940 --> 00:01:58.020
Read actively.

23
00:01:58.700 --> 00:02:03.340
Identify each text's central ideas,
notice viewpoint and reliability,

24
00:02:03.940 --> 00:02:07.540
and support every inference with
relevant evidence from the text.

25
00:02:08.260 --> 00:02:11.500
The first language focus is Partitive Expressions.

26
00:02:12.220 --> 00:02:14.760
What Are Partitive Expressions?

27
00:02:15.820 --> 00:02:19.420
Partitive expressions help you talk
about a portion or part of something.

28
00:02:20.020 --> 00:02:22.780
They make your sentences clearer and more specific.

29
00:02:23.440 --> 00:02:28.360
For example, instead of saying "I want
cake," you can say "I want a piece of cake."

30
00:02:29.040 --> 00:02:34.160
Instead of saying "She felt happiness,"
you can say "She felt a surge of happiness."

31
00:02:35.100 --> 00:02:40.240
These small phrases make a big difference in
how natural and precise your English sounds.

32
00:02:41.020 --> 00:02:47.060
Notice the structure in the model examples, then apply
it deliberately in connected sentences and paragraphs.

33
00:02:47.980 --> 00:02:52.740
In speaking, you will complete
Speaking 1: Vocabulary Expert Interview.

34
00:02:53.040 --> 00:02:57.380
Organise your ideas, use evidence
and respond clearly to questions.

35
00:02:58.100 --> 00:03:01.080
In writing, you will plan, draft, check and revise.

36
00:03:01.760 --> 00:03:04.870
Use the success criteria before submitting your work.

37
00:03:05.120 --> 00:03:06.220
You are ready to begin.

38
00:03:07.040 --> 00:03:13.240
Start with the vocabulary lab, continue through
reading and comprehension, apply the grammar focus,

39
00:03:13.240 --> 00:03:16.180
and complete the speaking and writing practices.

40
00:03:17.060 --> 00:03:22.240
Use AI English for hints and feedback, and
bring your questions to the live sessions.
